{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Workspace missing app paths causes deploy failure",
    "Explanation": [
      "The workflow shows all three build jobs (linux, mac, windows) succeeded, so builds_green is true. Each build job creates both app/\u003cplatform\u003e/app.\u003cplatform\u003e and meta/\u003cplatform\u003e/build.txt, but persist_to_workspace only lists meta/\u003cplatform\u003e. As a result, the deploy job's attach_workspace step only restores the meta files. The log's find output confirms this: it lists only ./meta/linux/build.txt, ./meta/mac/build.txt and ./meta/windows/build.txt, with no app files. The 'test -f app/linux/app.linux' check therefore fails with exit code 1, the 'Verify apps present' step fails, and the deploy job is marked FAILED (deploy_green false, workspace_had_apps false). The fix is to persist the application paths in each build job, for example adding 'app/linux', 'app/windows' and 'app/mac' to the respective persist_to_workspace paths with root '.'. The attach at '.' then restores app/\u003cplatform\u003e/app.\u003cplatform\u003e where the verify step and store_artifacts expect them. Other options do not work. Storing artifacts in the build jobs does not share files through the workspace. Fixing only one platform still leaves two tests failing. Changing only the attach location does not add files that were never persisted. Removing the verify step only hides the problem, since the apps would still be missing for upload."
